{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user's task is to implement srd025-unexpand requirements R1.1-R1.4 (default behavior - leading whitespace only) in `cmd/unexpand/main.go`. This is a \"stitch\" task (#5273) from the cobbler code generation pipeline for the go-unix-utils project. The task specifies:\n   - R1.1: Replace leading spaces with tabs when alignment permits (tabs preferred when spaces reach a tab stop exactly)\n   - R1.2: Non-leading whitespace must be written unchanged in default mode\n   - R1.3: Spaces that don't exactly reach a tab stop must stay as spaces (no overshooting)\n   - R1.4: Existing tab characters in leading whitespace count toward column position\n   - Must preserve contract stubs for R2.x-R4.x requirements\n   - Acceptance criteria: `go build` succeeds, `go vet` clean, behavior matches SRD\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU unexpand: converts spaces to tabs, by default only in leading whitespace\n   - Tab stop computation: 1-based column positions, default interval of 8\n   - `tabStops` struct with `interval` (uniform) or `positions` (explicit list)\n   - Differential testing against `gunexpand` (Homebrew GNU coreutils)\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Space-to-tab compaction: replace runs of spaces with tabs when they exactly reach a tab stop\n   - Column tracking: 1-based, tabs advance to next tab stop, newlines reset to 1\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd025-unexpand.yaml`\n     - Full SRD with requirements R1-R4, non-goals, and acceptance criteria\n     - R1 (Default behavior): R1.1-R1.4 cover leading whitespace conversion\n     - R2 (All whitespace -a): R2.1-R2.3 cover -a flag behavior\n     - R3 (Custom tab stops -t):